                    "text": "The PAINT Act aligns with S.1717\u2014the Ensuring Patient Access to Critical Breakthrough Products Act\u2014which mandates Medicare coverage for breakthrough devices during a 4-year transitional period. While streamlining access is critical, the $10M annual funding allocation for CMS program management (Sec.2(c)) raises questions about bureaucratic overhead versus direct patient benefit.\n\nTrue efficiency requires sunsetting redundant approval layers entirely, not just creating new compliance checkpoints. Medicare\u2019s track record of delayed national coverage determinations (Sec.1862(l)(2)) proves more structural reform is needed beyond procedural tweaks.\n\nCutting red tape shouldn\u2019t mean shuffling it through different agency desks. Let\u2019s audit implementation costs in real-time to ensure savings actually reach patients instead of feeding administrative bloat.\n\nThe real test is whether these reforms deliver care or just more paperwork\u2014see the full analysis: https://t.co/plA9UGO6sM",
